  {
   "type": "Feature",
   "properties": {
    "id": 1,
    "name": "Redsand Lake",
    "kind": "lake",
    "source": "manual",
    "note": "DFO Region 6 scope B(ii) regulates 'Redsand Lake' including tributaries (coho 4/day only 1 over 50 cm Sep 1-Oct 31; no fishing for chinook all year). FWA has no polygon for it, so no water of that name exists at all — an exact lookup for 'Redsand Lake' returns nothing. Treston Lake, 441 m south, carries the name variant 'TRESTON LAKE  REDSAND LAKE' from a BATHYMETRY map label (source: bathymetry in name_variants.json) — a sheet covering both lakes, which is itself evidence they are two waters. It indexes only under its own full string, so Treston never answered to 'Redsand Lake'; a substring search suggests otherwise and is not how the matcher works. Sits on the Kitsumkalum River (blk 360883243, wsc 400-195432) in the section 'between Treston Lake and Kitsumkalum Lake' — the same river Treston sits on, 441 m north of it. Hand-drawn, supplied by the curator 2026-09-01, EPSG:3857 -> 4326. 40.49 ha, 25 vertices, centre 54.70592/-128.77963, MU 6-15. Derived ids: id 1 -> wbk -1, gnis -9000001 — both NEGATIVE, and the gnis is beyond the real range in magnitude (real gnis run 1,642..8,000,027) so it cannot be confused with a real id even if a sign is lost.",
