    "kind": "lake",
    "source": "osm",
    "note": "The ungazetted 'Mission Creek Regional Park Children's Fishing Pond' that the Region 8 MU 8-10 override 'HALL ROAD (Mission) POND' names ALONGSIDE FWA waterbody 329460964 — two distinct ponds 194 m apart in the same park, both inside the regulated area. Only the FWA one had geometry; this one was a bare point (-119.42958, 49.87084). Polygon supplied by the curator from OpenStreetMap way 302989664 v1 (name='Children's Fishing Pond', natural=water, water=pond): 11 vertices, 0.22 ha, centre 49.87084/-119.42959, EPSG:4326. The curated point falls INSIDE it. Kept under its OWN name, NOT 'Hall Road Pond': 329460964 already carries the curated name 'HALL ROAD POND' (name_variants, source 'regulation') and is the only item that normalises to 'hall road pond' in MU 8-10 — a second one would make that lookup ambiguous and the matcher would drop it to UNMATCHED. The override pins BOTH wbks instead, and an override always beats name matching. Isolated water: no stream fid overlaps it (nearest piece is Mission Creek, blk 356569550, 539 m away), so it claims nothing and splits nothing. Derived ids: id 3 -> wbk -3, gnis -9000003.",
